1. What is DevOps?
Ans: DevOps is a combination of Development and Operations.
It helps development and operations teams work together efficiently.
DevOps uses automation, continuous integration, and continuous deployment.
It helps deliver software faster and with better reliability.
It also improves collaboration and communication between teams.

========================================================================================================================
2. Difference between DevOps & traditional model?
Ans: 

DevOps Model:

DevOps focuses on collaboration between development and operations teams. It uses automation, continuous testing, continuous integration, and continuous deployment. This helps deliver software faster and provides continuous feedback and monitoring.

Traditional Model:

In the traditional model, development and operations teams work separately. It relies more on manual processes and follows a sequential approach. Testing and deployment usually happen after development is completed, making the process slower.

