3. Write 5 Linux commands

Ans: Practiced Following Linux commands:

pwd – Shows the current working directory.
ls – Lists files and folders in the current directory.
cd folder – Moves into the specified folder.
cd .. – Moves to the parent directory.
mkdir test – Creates a new directory named test.
touch file.txt – Creates a new empty file named file.txt.
rm file.txt – Deletes the specified file.
rm -r test – Deletes the specified folder and its contents.
cat file.txt – Displays the contents of a file.

